y hand is very weak (one pair of 10s with Ace kicker). The opponent's river raise after checking through all streets suggests they either have a legitimate hand or are bluffing a missed draw. However, with such a weak holding, I'm behind most value betting ranges. The pot is small (only a few hundred chips), and calling 300 when I likely have the worst hand is not worth it. Given I'm ahead overall in the match, preserving chips and avoiding marginal spots is the prudent strategy.\n\nAnswer: -1"}
